# D35 (docs/define-gorget/decisions.md, ratified 2026-07-26): an unnamed
# parameter's sigil in a function type goes AFTER the type
# (`Callable[void(int &)]`), mirroring the named-parameter rule
# (`void modify(Message &msg)`). The pre-D35 spelling with the sigil
# BEFORE the type (`Callable[void(&int)]`) is REJECTED at parse — never
# co-accepted (D32's close-the-enumeration-by-construction thesis).
#
# The parser must emit `FunctionTypeParamSigilBeforeType` with a
# teaching diagnostic naming the replacement spelling. This fixture
# uses PARAM-position (`Callable[void(&int)] cb`) — a non-speculative
# parse context where the D35 diagnostic surfaces directly (the
# local-decl case A1 is filed separately). Fixture lives in its own
# directory so the unparseable source stays OUT of the top-level
# fixture sweeps (fmt_idempotent, *_comparison, runtime_diff).
void modify(int &x):
    x = 42

void call_it(Callable[void(&int)] cb, int &y):
    cb(&y)

void main():
    int y = 5
    call_it(modify, &y)
    print(y)
